Beryllium: no swap file for renderers (page data stays in memory)

Purpose: for every renderer of a normal (not Incognito) profile,
  RenderProcessHostImpl::ProvideSwapFileForRenderer() creates a file in
  the temporary directory (base::CreateTemporaryFile, so
  /tmp/.org.chromium.Chromium.XXXXXX), opens it read-write with
  FLAG_DELETE_ON_CLOSE, which on POSIX unlinks it at once, and hands it to
  the renderer's blink::DiskDataAllocator. Blink writes compressed parked
  strings (scripts and other large strings of background tabs; parking to
  disk is on wherever kCompressParkableStrings is, which includes Linux and
  FreeBSD) and parked images into it. The owner's runs of 0.20.3.6 (5
  November 2026) found it: after the memfd change, each renderer still
  held one writable regular file with no name, 0 bytes, mode -rw-------,
  held by no other process (fstat), with every Capsicum right; renderers
  looked nothing up in /tmp, while the browser looked up
  /tmp/.org.chromium.Chromium.XXXXXX 63 times for about 21 renderers,
  three lookups per file (create, open, unlink), as this function does.
  That is page content on a disk file system and a writable file a
  confined renderer would keep (S-REN-06).
  This patch skips the file unless the feature BerylliumRendererSwapFile
  is enabled (--enable-features=BerylliumRendererSwapFile). Without the
  file, DiskDataAllocator never writes (may_write_ stays false) and parked
  data stays compressed in memory: exactly what Chromium does for every
  Incognito renderer, and what the code says the renderer handles ("the
  renderer will not wait for one"). The cost is the memory those
  compressed strings and images would have freed.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). No dependency on other patches; applies after
  Helium's bromite/fingerprinting-flags-client-rects-and-measuretext.patch,
  which touches the same file elsewhere.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench. Not yet
  compiled.
Test: freebsd/tests/browser/tests/test_50_sandbox.py
  test_renderers_hold_no_directories_or_writable_files (no unnamed writable
  file left in any renderer); the Capsicum survey's temporary files section
  (no /tmp/.org.chromium.Chromium.XXXXXX lookups by the browser).
security-review: not required (removes a file handed to an untrusted
  process; no new input handling)

--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
@@ -1287,6 +1287,15 @@
 BASE_FEATURE(kUserVisibleProcessPriority, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 #endif
 
+// Beryllium (plan/14-RENDERER-SANDBOX.md, feature matrix S-REN-06): no swap
+// file for renderers unless this feature is enabled. The file is created in
+// the temporary directory, unlinked at once and handed to the renderer, which
+// writes compressed page data (parked strings and images) into it under
+// memory pressure: page content on disk, and a writable file a confined
+// renderer would keep. Without it Blink keeps that data compressed in memory,
+// as it already does in Incognito windows.
+BASE_FEATURE(kBerylliumRendererSwapFile, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+
 // Please keep in sync with "RenderProcessHostBlockedURLReason" in
 // tools/metrics/histograms/metadata/browser/enums.xml. These values are
 // persisted to logs. Entries should not be renumbered and numeric values should
@@ -6495,6 +6504,10 @@
   // In Incognito, nothing should be written to disk. Don't provide a file..
   if (GetBrowserContext()->IsOffTheRecord())
     return;
+  // Beryllium: in no window, unless asked for (see kBerylliumRendererSwapFile).
+  if (!base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kBerylliumRendererSwapFile)) {
+    return;
+  }
 
   mojo::Remote<blink::mojom::DiskAllocator> allocator;
   BindReceiver(allocator.BindNewPipeAndPassReceiver());
